diff --git a/docs/business-rules.md b/docs/business-rules.md
index d72c8c7..045d72a 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -100,6 +100,14 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); AuthZ stays out of scope per #20 and HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
 
+### Queue Lifecycle and Access
+
+* **Queue creation, update, and deactivation** are managed by entity owners and admins. Queues are created with a unique slug within the entity and are active by default. They can be renamed, have their slug updated, or deactivated (`is_active = false`). Deactivation prevents issuance or calling of tickets but preserves existing tickets.
+* **Access grants** are controlled via the `queue_access` table. Managers can grant or revoke the `call` permission to any employee membership within the same entity. Granting creates or updates a row; revoking deletes it.
+* **Authorization** is governed by `App\Policies\QueuePolicy`. Owners and admins may create, update, and manage access for queues. Employees may call tickets from a queue only if they possess a `queue_access` row with the `call` permission for that queue.
+
+### End of rules
+
 ### Priority
 
 Priority is an **integer**: the **higher the value, the more prioritized**. Named levels are configurable presets per entity that map to values; ordering uses the number, not the label.
